#
# To maximize r, include the boundary in the compact feasible set.
# Boundary products are zero; a positive candidate below has r > 0.
# At any positive maximizer, the constraint gradients are independent
# (dependence would require x=y=z, inconsistent with q=14).
# Lagrange multipliers for log(xyz) imply
# 1/t = lambda + mu*(9-t) for each t in {x,y,z}.
# This nonzero quadratic has at most two roots, so two variables coincide.
